2026-10-10T23:42:13.9384459Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9459111Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9466871Z [0m
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9467281Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9467755Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9467875Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9468262Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9468702Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9468932Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9469141Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9469570Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9469767Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9470237Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9470826Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9471206Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9471505Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9471609Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9471731Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9471869Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9472138Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9472336Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9472413Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9472481Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9472566Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9472768Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9473041Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9477900Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9477983Z I will:
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9478049Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9478164Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9478395Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9478640Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9478854Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9479056Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9479295Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9479658Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9479968Z    /root
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9522184Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9522629Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9531208Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9531752Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9531995Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9534522Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9534868Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9547544Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9548230Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9555970Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9556438Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9556702Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9556819Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9556924Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9557046Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9557191Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9557596Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9557719Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9557780Z If you would like to
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9557934Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9558028Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9558136Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9558320Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9558401Z 
2026-10-10T23:42:13.9558411Z 
